<!-- The CA4 brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the typst
     template (Times New Roman, FRAP 32(a)(5)(A)) at 14 pt (size 28 half points), Body Text in 25.9 pt line boxes
     with a half-inch indent, footnotes 14 pt in 16 pt boxes, exact line spacing (typst pitch-double, pitch-single);
     then the "CA ..." paragraph styles ca4.lua writes the cover, headings, tables and certificates in, single-spaced
     (16 pt boxes), with the typst template's spaces: section headings 21 pt above and 15.4 pt below, centered bold
     capitals (CASectionBig: 16 pt type); unnumbered sub-headings 16.8 / 12.6 pt; numbered ones 15.4 / 12.6 pt, the
     label at S half-inches, the text hanging a half inch more, no heading level italic (typst style-heading); the contents' page column 36 pt (720), the
     authorities' 56 pt (1120), the text width 6.5 in (9360), the right half from 4680. No keep-with-next on headings
     (ca4.lua moves a heading a pass left at the foot of a page instead: typst's sticky headings). The page setup,
     sections and footers come from ca4.lua and fb render (docxpass.rs). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
